    "body": "Hi echasnovski.\r\n\r\nThe `doc` variable inside `H.normalize_item_doc` function could be a table in some case, like when `lsp_item.documentation= { kind = \"markdown\" }` , which it should always be a string, otherwise it will throw an error while calling `doc:find`.\r\nfixed by adjust the `doc` variable assignment statement.\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\nI encountered this problem when using mini.completion with [kulala.nvim](https://github.com/mistweaverco/kulala.nvim), this plugin include a kulala LSP:\r\n<img width=\"1226\" height=\"974\" alt=\"Snipaste_2025-08-06_14-20-28\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a1eab5de-5092-415c-965b-c43aa4f55e56\" />\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2025-08-06T13:24:41Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nBy the quick looks of it, the current implementation is more safe, because:\r\n- Supplying documentation as a table with only `kind` and no `value` does not follow the LSP specification. The value should be [`MarkupContent`](https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/specifications/lsp/3.17/specification/#markupContentInnerDefinition) which requires both fields present.\r\n- The `documentation` (if present) [may also be string directly](https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/specifications/lsp/3.17/specification/#completionItem), which the change in the PR stops account for.\r\n\r\nCould you please provide a minimal reproduction example so that I can see in more details on what is going on? My current understanding is that it is an issue with either LSP server or 'kulala.nvim'.",
