        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> This indeed solves the problem and also complies with the relevant LSP specifications. So are you planning to make these changes in mini.completion? I’m fine with whatever you decide, but I personally prefer making these changes. Some LSP implementations may not handle null and empty strings well, and these changes many make the handling of `doc.value` more robust.\r\n\r\nThe general idea is that 'mini.completion' will not make *substantial* extra efforts to account for LSP servers that don't follow the specification. Otherwise it will become to convoluted. Specification exists to introduce a standard which simplifies implementations of both LSP server (no need to invent custom solutions and data structures) and LSP client (it can assume specific data structures in specific situations).\r\n\r\nBut since in this particular instance it was already accounted for (just not covering all the issues), I'll adjust it soon (probably tomorrow).",
            "created_at": "2025-08-06T12:24:23Z",
